Good afternoon,

We are instructed to notify a dropped-load incident on the Rivergate Commons Phase II project. Our reference is AV/BR/2025/3358.

Policy number: BR-3358-20471
Project name: Rivergate Commons Phase II
Contract number: AIA-A102-2025-RGC2
Insured name: Rivergate Development Partners, LLC
Date of loss: 26 February 2026
Loss location: 2650 Rivergate Parkway, Charlotte, NC 28273
Estimated loss: USD 407,200

A bundle of engineered joists being flown to Level 4 caught a 41 mph gust, swung
into the Level 3 frame and then dropped to the podium when the choker slipped.
Nobody was hurt - the exclusion zone was maintained and the site cleared per the
lift plan. It is not OSHA reportable.

The podium deck has two impact craters, one with exposed prestressing strand,
and the engineer has shored the bay and will not release it pending coring. A
26-foot section of Level 3 wall is racked and comes down.

This is a first-party loss to the works. There is no third-party injury and no
damage to anyone else's property, so our client's liability policy is not
engaged and we are not notifying it.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * structural engineer's report
  * reinstatement schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. The failed choker, the slings
and the load chart have been bagged and retained, and nothing has been cleared.

